WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.759
Film Courage: Common misconceptions about
what a writer should do after their script

00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:04.759
is finished?

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:08.120
Travis Seppala, Screenwriter/Author: Let’s
see one is getting your script registered

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.750
with the WGA [Writers Guild of America] versus
having it copyrighted versus mailing it to

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:13.750
yourself.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.260
I’ve seen many writers who still believe
that if you mail your script to yourself that

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.260
counts as a copyright.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.260
No it does not.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.810
It will not hold up in court.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.519
The only thing that will hold in court is
a copyright where it has an official document

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:29.849
attached and said this script was copyrighted
on this date.&nbsp;

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:35.020
WGA registration is still better than mailing
it to yourself but it’s not quite as good

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:42.280
as a copyright especially with the way they
change their registration and stuff only goes

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.280
like overall.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.620
It doesn’t go per draft.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.290
Whereas with copyrighting you’re going to
want to copyright each thing that way you

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.290
get proof of it.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:53.150
It’s a little more expensive to copyright
but it’s the safest thing if one of those

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.310
very rare stealings ever happen.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:58.070
Film Courage: What is a paranoid screenwriter?

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:01.050
Travis: People who are afraid their stuff
is going to get taken.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.010
People who won’t send their stuff out to
competitions, won’t send their stuff out

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.610
to producers without an NDA.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:11.170
Never send an NDA to a producer and be like
“Oh you can’t read my script until…”

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:15.080
No, they will just give you your NDA back
and be like “Well I don’t need to read

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.720
your script.”

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.360
Which I have met several people who think
that they need to send an NDA out in order

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.360
to get a producer to read…no.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.630
The producer is not going to sign the NDA.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.460
You need to sign an NDA for the producer possibly
if you want to work on the project that they’re

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.270
needing to hire a writer for to save their
butts.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:35.800
You are not going to take their idea and go
write it yourself without them.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.930
But they will not sign an NDA for you.&nbsp;

